    "turn_text": "and welcome to this edition of Soul Force Politics, Radical Love, Radical Change. I'm your host, Heather Mizzier, and today's guest spent 29 years as a professor of constitutional law at American University's Washington College of Law before he was elected to the U.S. Congress in 2016. You might be familiar with his dazzling intellect while watching the House impeachment hearings where he serves as a well-regarded member of the House Judiciary Committee. Congressman Jamie Raskin joins us on today's show to share his brilliant insights into the foundations of our democracy and what is at stake for the future of America's experiment with self-governance. For many years, Jamie and I were neighbors in Tacoma Park, Maryland. I had the honor of serving with him in the Maryland General Assembly for eight years. Jamie Raskin was a state senator representing the same district that I served as a member of the House. We were a team, elected together, and I thoroughly enjoyed our time pushing for a range of progressive new laws in Annapolis from 2007 to 2015. We share the belief that elected officials are public servants. I could not be more thrilled that he is now shining his light in the halls of Congress.",
