    "turn_text": "without being a Trump hater. You're going to love this conversation, which runs the gamut of the Federalist Papers to Speaker Pelosi's decision to hold the Articles of Impeachment until a proper Senate trial is assured, from questions of abuse of power to violations of the foreign and domestic emolluments clause, with so many impeachable offenses. Why were the House articles limited to just two instances? From aggression to forbearance, what is the role of restraint in party governance? Do we need political parties? Are some senators risking jury nullification? Oh yes, all of this and so much more. Especially don't miss the very last 10 minutes of this interview where Congressman Jamie Raskin and I share an incredible sole force politics moment together. And a little foreign policy cheat sheet for anyone that's not familiar with all the names of the foreign leaders that the congressman references in our conversation. Victor Orban is the prime minister of Hungary. Vladimir Putin, the president of Russia. Vladimir Zelensky, president of Ukraine. Rodrigo Duterte, president of the Philippines. Abdel Fattah, LCC, president of Egypt. As always, we deeply appreciate your support for our work at Soul Force Politics. Be sure to follow us on social media and remember to share this podcast with your network, subscribe on your favorite podcast application, and rate and review the show so others will learn of our great conversations that inspire radical love, radical change. Our production costs are entirely supported through generous listeners like you. So please help us continue to keep the show high quality and commercial free. You can make your tax exempt donation on our support page at www.soulforcepolitics.org. And without further delay, here's our interview. Congressman Jamie Raskin, I am thrilled beyond measure to be here with you today because you're one of my most favorite humans in the whole world. It has been my distinct honor and just a load of fun to be your friend and your colleague over a number of years, having served in the Maryland General Assembly together. to watch you take your particular form of brilliant political analysis and constitutional law expertise, but with this giant heart that you have into the Congress that needs all of those things right now. Thank you so much for being on the",
