    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92347.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 15,
    "turn_text": "Well, it is fragile. It is vulnerable. Lincoln knew that when he stood at the Gettysburg battlefield and asked whether government of the people by the people for the people show perish from the earth. I mean, he meant that. You correctly describe it as an experiment. It was a very young experiment then, but it's still a young experiment now and all over the world. democracies under attack and authoritarianisms on the march and you know you've got people like Orban who says that we're moving into the period of history for illiberal democracy meaning democracy without rights basically mob rule where minority rights are being trampled So all that's really left of democracies, the shell of the TV audience that gets to applaud the despots and the dictators who go about violating the rights of minorities and immigrants and women and gay people and so on. That's what they mean by it. Vladimir Putin has said that liberalism is extinct and is vanishing. And so all over the world, the idea of democracies under attack, and Donald Trump is right there with them. I mean, he never has a positive word to say about democracy or the Founding Fathers or the Constitution. He's not interested in it. I mean, for him, It's a mass TV audience that's there to be simply mobilized and deployed for purposes of persecuting minorities and increasingly engaging in hate against other countries. That's where we are now. He's brought us to the brink of war with Iran. It's a very 1984 situation right now.",
