  {
    "episode_id": 92347,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92347.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 16,
    "turn_text": "I want to come back to that, the current situation that we're facing with Iran, staying on our conversation about threats for democracy. Democracy really is only alive when we can engage with each other about civic issues in a civil way. And that really feels upended right now. We're no longer just disagreeing about tax policy and health care and guns in the environment. The divisions are deeper now. They are going beyond policy and seem to be more about political identity and protection of power. And there are people who call themselves patriots, but who are defending actions that are undermining our tenets of democracy. And some of what I want your input on includes these things that aren't just about democracy's threat for minorities and people that governmental institutions are meant to protect, but the government institutions themselves are threatened, right? When you have subpoenas that are being ignored when you're using the Justice Department as a political tool, when you're declaring a national emergency to circumvent Congress to get the funding for your border wall, undermining the credibility of independent journalism, these are really chipping away at the foundational elements of How our government even exists to then create those protections for the people that you are in Congress fighting for every day?",
