  {
    "episode_id": 92347,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92347.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 17,
    "turn_text": "Absolutely. And look, we don't want to overly romanticize the past because everything that you just talked about, a free press, civic respect, all of these things have been hard won battles. efforts, obviously, to make America about racism or about slavery, America is about male supremacy and so on. And it's been social struggles and constitutional amendments and litigation and protests that have transformed America and turned us into something far better than all of that. But what's remarkable now is that you have one entire political party and a president in an entire administration that are devoted to turning the clock back on everything, they describe the press as the enemy of the people. I mean, Thomas Jefferson said that the press was the people's best friend. He were forced to choose between having a government without a newspaper, or a newspaper without a government, he would not hesitate a moment to choose the latter. The newspaper gives the people the information they need to govern themselves, and a government without a newspaper is a dangerous situation because what you get is state power and no check against it. But all of these things are under attack. The right to vote is under attack with voter suppression and voter purges, wherever Republicans are in control of state governments across the country. Elections themselves are under attack by foreign sabotage and cyber attack in espionage. We have civil rights under attack. We have women's reproductive freedoms under attack in many states throughout the union. You name it. We are facing a full-scale assault on the civilizing movements of the last century or more, the civil rights movement, the women's movement, the LGBT movement, the peace movement, the human rights movement, the labor movement, all of them are under severe attack right now. And your point is correct that Donald Trump and Mitch McConnell and their friends are using every conceivable lever of power of undemocratic power to stay in control, whether it's the Electoral College, whether it's gerrymandering of the congressional districts, whether it's voter suppression, whether it's packing the courts with right-wing judges, they have all of the plays in the authoritarian playbook.",
