  {
    "episode_id": 92347,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92347.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 21,
    "turn_text": "I think there's something, too, that I just got back from a conference at Harvard with those guys with Levitsky and the how democracies die crowd. And their critical value, of course, is forbearance, which is mentioned in that passage there, that political parties have to operate with a sense of self-restraint, so that it's not rule or ruin. And I do think there is a rule or ruin mentality that the Republicans have. You know, when Barack Obama was elected president, Mitch McConnell said that his chief in overriding goal was to prevent Obama from getting anything done on his agenda. And they said with Donald Trump, of course, that Obama was not even a U.S. citizen and they had this birther conspiracy that just never ended. And they impeached Bill Clinton for telling one lie about sex, which was a low crime in misdemeanor. But generally, they do pursue a rule or ruin philosophy. And I hope that that we can stand up for the rule of law and stand up for the Constitution in a way that has integrity, that doesn't show hate, that doesn't advertise contempt for anybody, but that is also tough because we are trying to defend the democracy. That's a tough thing to do. But one thing that really got to me during the impeachment process was when Congressman Jim Jordan from Ohio said that the Democrats hated the millions of people who voted for Donald Trump, which is an outrageous character assassination on us. I mean, for one thing, lots of people on our side have members of our families who are Republicans who voted for Trump. We have people in our districts who voted for Trump. We don't hate those people. That's like Trump telling Nancy Pelosi that she hates him. She doesn't hate him. And when she said she prays for him, she does pray for him. That's real. And then he told her, no, she wasn't praying for him. He knows people and everybody's saying that she's not really praying for him. I know Nancy Pelosi and Nancy Pelosi is praying for Donald Trump. And I was asked the same question whether I hated Donald Trump. I don't hate him at all. I pity him. I think he has a tortured mind. depraved heart, but I don't hate him. I fear a lot more the people around him who have continued to support and enable him",
