    "turn_idx": 25,
    "turn_text": "Well, I should say that there are lots of members of our caucus who are showing more forbearance in patience than I would be. In other words, I think that there are many more impeachable offenses that we have overwhelming evidence of that were not brought forward. And I think that there were more conservative members of our caucus who felt as if This category of impeachable offense is relating to national security, relating to the president, trying to dragoon a foreign government to come into our election, or the ones that are the narrowest and would have, therefore, the broadest possible popular appeal. From the very beginning, I felt that the president is in direct defiance and violation of the foreign emoluments clause by collecting millions of dollars from foreign governments in continuing to operate his hotels and his resorts and his various businesses, and he's been in violation of the domestic emoluments clause by collecting money at his resorts from U.S. government and federal agencies and departments. Every time they go down to Mar-a-Lago, they spend another 150 or $200,000 from the Department of Defense, the Department of State, the White House, the FBI, the Secret Service, and so on. And the president is forbidden under the domestic appointments clause to receive any money from the US government in the federal tax payers other than a salary. He says he doesn't take his salary. That's the only money he's allowed to take. He can't take the other stuff. He should take his salary and leave the other millions of dollars alone. But in any event, I would go much further. I think that",
