    "turn_idx": 35,
    "turn_text": "articles out. Well, yeah, I mean, in other words, if it's a high crime in misdemeanor, then let's bring it out. Whereas I think Speaker Pelosi is much more focused on, she understands the lawlessness of this president. She knows that he's a one-man crime wave, but she's thinking, what is it that will have the broadest possible consensus behind it? And what the president did was absolutely outrageous. No president's done anything like that before, holding up hundreds of millions of dollars in foreign military assistance to a besieged ally in order to extract an agreement from the president to come and get involved in his presidential election to support him. I mean, that's just unspeakable. And it violates every premise of the impeachment clause. The reason we've got an impeachment clause is the founders did not want presidents dragging foreign powers into our elections. They didn't want the president elevating his personal financial interests above the common good. And they didn't want the president corrupting our elections.",
