    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92347.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 37,
    "turn_text": "Well, I was not surprised because, you know, welcome to my world. I've been living this for three years now in Congress. Almost everything is like that. Almost everything of real consequence and substantial weight is like that where we get this extraordinary partisan divide. And it's frustrating and you feel like you're just caught in it and it's very tough to know how to break out of it. For me, talking about the Constitution and the framers and the history of our Constitution is the way that I try to build a bridge and find a common ground to stand on with them. But once they get their talking points, they get going and they just stick with it and they repeat it and it's very hard to get them to engage in a real dialogue where You speak and I listen to you and I speak and you listen to me and we go back and forth and we may disagree, but we're at least responding to each",
