    "turn_idx": 65,
    "turn_text": "Exactly right. I don't think there's anything wrong with the senators saying, look, we understand this is a public process. It's not like a jury which is not supposed to know anything about the facts of case. Obviously the whole country knows about what's going on. All they're saying really is the House of Representatives has found sufficient evidence, in this case sufficient and uncontradicted evidence that the president committed high crimes and misdemeanors. That's a serious issue that leads to a trial. But now in the trial, the managers will have to make a case to the satisfaction of the Senate under the Senate's rules. And the president will have an opportunity to make a full-blown defense to bring on whatever witnesses he wants. And this is why we've been urging a real trial process that includes witnesses",
