    "turn_idx": 80,
    "turn_text": "about that other you said check and balance and I love that because I went back and we looked at where the phrase checks and balances appears because people think it's all about the executive and the judicial and the legislative. Actually checks and balances appears just once in the Federalist Papers and it relates to the House and the Senate. You know, I found that because I've been trying to challenge this whole idea that we've got three co-equal branches, which I think is a total misunderstanding of the constitutional design. You know, our forebears overthrew a king. They wanted to create government by the people, and that means the people's representatives, and the Congress was made Article 1 for a reason, because it is the law-making power, and the President's job is just to take care that the laws are faithfully executed and to be Commander-in-Chief of the Army and Navy in times of actual, you know, insurrection or conflict. But other than that, I mean, the President really has an executing job to execute the laws that have been adopted by us. And as I've been saying everywhere, there's a reason that Congress has the power to impeach the President, but the President doesn't have the power to impeach the Congress. The framers feared, above all, a President becoming a tyrant and a despot.",
