    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92347.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 81,
    "turn_text": "I want to go back to this notion of John Roberts sitting as the Chief Justice of the Supreme Court presiding over the trial. The House ultimately didn't try to compel witness appearances during the impeachment phase because there would have been a delay due to the appeals process. Is there a sense that Senate Democrats will be able to compel witnesses to appear at the trial phase because Judge Roberts would theoretically be able to rule on it immediately?",
