  {
    "episode_id": 92347,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92347.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 82,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, I think that there would be a lot more dispatch because they'd be in the trial period, because the Chief Justice would be there. And given that the President has already been impeached, I think that they would no longer have an interest in trying to drag things out and blockade all the witnesses and prevent the testimony from coming in. sort of shifted the burden at this point. You can kind of see that right now in the dynamics between Speaker Pelosi and President Trump. I mean, he's been impeached, and so he's freaking out about the situation to the extent that he's tried to wag the dog and engage in assassination of a foreign military general in Iran. So it's a dangerous moment here. I think we all have an interest in moving this quickly so that the President doesn't continue to compound his criminality and corruption.",
