        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "Congress holds the constitutional power to declare war.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "Historically, monarchs often initiated wars for vanity or political advantage.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Monarchs used war to divert public attention from domestic issues.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "The Founding Fathers opposed the practice of monarchs starting wars arbitrarily.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "The Founding Fathers viewed uncontrolled warfare as wasteful and dangerous.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "War should involve a formal cost-benefit analysis before proceeding.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Representatives elected by the people should conduct the cost-benefit evaluation of war.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "American soldiers are citizens whose lives are at risk in conflicts.",
