    "turn_text": "That's absolutely right. And this was not anything that Congress undertook. We had not declared war against Iran. The president didn't even consult us. So if it wasn't war, it was assassination. But we don't use assassination for very excellent reasons of principle and prudence as an instrument of our foreign policy.",
