    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92347.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 110,
    "turn_text": "Well, in some sense, the Constitution followed Washington's advice, as you know, the Constitution doesn't mention political parties. And so everything that is developed around the regulation of political parties has been of a statutory nature. But I don't know that you can ever put the genie back in the bottle. I mean, George Washington had a fairly unique set of political skills and a political stature. You know, he was the last president ever elected with the entire electoral college on his side. You know.",
