    "turn_idx": 117,
    "turn_text": "Lives Matter and the indivisible groups which have been amazing all over America. So, you know, I think for me the context of The rebirth of democracy was created by the women's march of Washington. The very day after Trump was inaugurated, you know, on January 21st, 2017, that march and assembly said it all to me, you know, Millions of people across the country coming out in just the glorious diversity and creativity of our country to say, we're not going back and to assert the proper relationship between the people and the government in American democracy. All of us who aspire and attain to public office for whatever period of time are nothing but the servants of the people. And we're not the masters of the people in the moment. We think we're the masters of the people. It's time to evict, eject, reject, impeach, convict, remove, start again. And any of us in public office is easily dispensable. And it's the people and the society itself that matter. So, I think we're going to come back, but it does require us to keep that tok-villain point in mind. We have structural problems in our democracy. We have got to deal with the Electoral College, which has given us two popular vote losers in the last five elections. It has proven to be very manipulable and very malleable. We've got to deal with the gerrymandering of our congressional districts. I was proud that we passed that in the House of Representatives in HR1 to have independent redistricting commissions in every state. I hope we get to a point where we cannot just have independent redistricting commissions, but multi-member districts so that And rank choice voting. And rank choice voting. I mean, these are the technical changes we need to make that will empower all of America to be represented in a powerful way. There are ways to make this happen. You know, we can end voter suppression. We can have universal voter registration. That's something that needs to be done. That is the alternative to Trump. Trump is now in artifact. He's a relic. He's an antique of a series of decrepit political arrangements that we have to leave in the past. And we've got to move forward to a stronger, better, fuller, more complete democracy.",
