    "turn_text": "So, look, I'm a middle child. I like to bring people together, and I want to believe the best I want to try to bring out the best in myself and my friends and people across the aisle. I don't believe most people are fundamentally jerks. I don't believe most people are fascists and racists and misogynists. I don't think most people think that grabbing other people's genitals is a proper form of social introduction. And I would not attribute that to the vast majority of people. That's just not true. And so I think we've got a lot to work with. And societies like other institutions and other people go through tough times. We're just going through a tough time here. And I hope that the party that I work with, the Democratic Party, can try to stand for the best. But I would never confuse my party with moral virtue in any way. And I would not confuse any political Party with that, I would not confuse any state or society with that. States have been guilty of a lot of very grievous offenses against people all over the world. And so what we can hope to do is build societies and states that are as good as the people who make them up and who depend on them to survive.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
