    "turn_idx": 124,
    "turn_text": "And that's my hope for the Congress and why I had to take a moment, a sole force politics moment with you because you're, as I mentioned at the very beginning of the show, one of the biggest, most generous, hearted politicians I have had the honor to know. That's one of the reasons why our friendship was so real and genuine and why we connected so deeply. You always have a beautiful thing to say about somebody. I've never heard you behind the scenes be negative or diminishing of anyone's spirit in any way. You always call us to our better angels. And I hope that you might be able to take a little assignment from me to do whatever you can one by one within that institution. It feels big at 435 and yet in some ways that's a nice targeted group because if we can start getting people within Congress to see the value of connecting to each other's hearts and seeing each other's humanity and finding compassion in the conversations and really being curious about what the other one believes and thinks instead of just immediately rejecting it. There is the consciousness for change in both directions. Democrats have things that we can learn from Republicans on how to improve certain aspects of policies and Republicans have things they can learn from Democrats, but none of that is happening right now because it's just all in a place of dividing lines. And the only place those dividing lines are going to start coming down is from within. It's always where change happens from within. We have to go inside ourselves to make change before we can bring change out into the external world and it works the same within institutions. Congress itself someday can change. and rise to its highest self can govern with its light instead of its darkness but that's not what's happening right now because of these divisions and if anybody can go in and start creating these little opportunities for a shift for bringing in that kind of light. I think it's Jamie",
